CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1773713032
OL,1,T]St000p4p0p0t  <4,4V]D            A4/25
OL,2,T]S555555u5=%5  75 5V]DNEWS FROM
OL,3,T]S#!#!#!,%#!#  #! !V]DBBC CEEFAX
OL,4,V ||||||||||||||||||
OL,5,F
OL,6, The basic rate of income tax is to be
OL,7, reduced by 2p to 27 per cent, Mr Nigel
OL,8, Lawson has announced.
OL,10,FHe said the reduction would be worth
OL,11,Fmore than #3 a week to a man on average
OL,12,Fearnings.
OL,14,FHe proposed a corresponding cut in the
OL,15,Fsmall companies' rate of Corporation
OL,16,FTax from 29 per cent to 27 per cent.
OL,18,FHe said the income tax changes would
OL,19,Ftake affect on the first pay day after
OL,20,FMay 17 and would cost a little more
OL,21,Fthan #2 billion in 1987-88.
OL,23,D]CFromF17-03-87C/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49605
SC,0005
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1773713032
OL,1,T]St000p4p0p0t  <4,4V]D            A5/25
OL,2,T]S555555u5=%5  75 5V]DNEWS FROM
OL,3,T]S#!#!#!,%#!#  #! !V]DBBC CEEFAX
OL,4,V ||||||||||||||||||
OL,5,F
OL,6, The Chancellor said he was raising all
OL,7, main tax thresholds by about 3.7%.
OL,9,S/FSingle person's allowance will rise
OL,10,Fby #90 to #2,425 and the married man's
OL,11,Fallowance by #140 to #3,795.
OL,13,S/FSingle age allowance will rise by
OL,14,F#110 to #2,960.
OL,16,S/FMarried age allowance up by #170 to
OL,17,F#4,675.
OL,19,S/FThreshold for 45% rate up by #200 to
OL,20,F#20,400.
OL,22,S/FHigher tax thresholds stay unchanged.
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49606
SC,0006
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1773713032
OL,1,T]St000p4p0p0t  <4,4V]D            A6/25
OL,2,T]S555555u5=%5  75 5V]DNEWS FROM
OL,3,T]S#!#!#!,%#!#  #! !V]DBBC CEEFAX
OL,4,V ||||||||||||||||||
OL,5,F
OL,6, Mr Lawson also announced an increase
OL,7, in the age allowance for the over-80s.
OL,9,FHe said the increase would be double
OL,10,Fthe statutory indexation.
OL,12,S/FSingle age allowance for the over-80s
OL,13,Fup #220 to #3,070.
OL,15,S/FMarried age allowance for over-80s up
OL,16,F#340 to #4,845.
OL,18,FMr Lawson said this would benefit about
OL,19,F400,000 taxpayers with 25,000 of them
OL,20,Fbeing taken out of the income tax
OL,21,Fsystem altogether.
OL,23,D]CFromF17-03-87C/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49607
SC,0007
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1773713032
OL,1,T]St000p4p0p0t  <4,4V]D           GA7/25
OL,2,T]S555555u5=%5  75 5V]DNEWS FROM
OL,3,T]S#!#!#!,%#!#  #! !V]DBBC CEEFAX
OL,4,V ||||||||||||||||||
OL,5,F
OL,6, Mr Lawson said he plans to increase the
OL,7, allowance for blind taxpayers.
OL,9,FThe blind person's allowance has not
OL,10,Fchanged since 1981 when it rose by #180
OL,11,Fto its present level of #340.
OL,13,FMr Lawson's proposal will increase the
OL,14,Fallowance for 1987-1988 by a further
OL,15,F#180 to #520.
OL,23,D]CFromF17-03-87C/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49608
SC,0008
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1773713032
OL,1,T]St000p4p0p0t  <4,4V]D           GA8/25
OL,2,T]S555555u5=%5  75 5V]DNEWS FROM
OL,3,T]S#!#!#!,%#!#  #! !V]DBBC CEEFAX
OL,4,V ||||||||||||||||||
OL,5,F
OL,6, There are to be no changes on duties
OL,7, on tobacco, drink or leaded petrol,
OL,8, Chancellor Mr Nigel Lawson announced.
OL,10,FHe said there was also to be no change
OL,11,Fon the #100 vehicle excise duty, but
OL,12,Fduty on unleaded petrol would be
OL,13,Flowered by five pence.
OL,14,F
OL,15,FScale charges for people with company
OL,16,Fcars are to be increased by 10 per
OL,17,Fcent for 1988-1989.
OL,19,FMr Lawson said he would abolish, from
OL,20,FMarch 29, the tax on on-course betting,
OL,21,Fbut the duty on the gaming machine
OL,22,Flicence would rise.
OL,23,                      D]CFromF17-03-87
