PN,49613
SC,0013
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1773713032
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     G13/25
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Members of the third largest teachers
OL,6, union in England and Wales have
OL,7, rejected a call for strike action.
OL,9,FThe Assistant Masters and Mistresses
OL,10,FAssociation voted by 56.7 per cent not
OL,11,Fto strike in protest at the pay
OL,12,Fsettlement imposed by the Government.
OL,14,FUnion president Mr Frank Groarke said
OL,15,Fthe ballot result did not mean the
OL,16,Funion accepted the Government's removal
OL,17,Fof teachers' negotiating rights.
OL,19,F"It shows that a majority reject
OL,20,Findustrial action as the most effective
OL,21,Fway to register protest," he said.
OL,23,T]CFrom 17-03-87 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
